A set X can be represented by an array x[n] as follows:Consider the following algorithm in which x,y and z are Boolean arrays of size n:algorithm zzz(x[] , y[], z []).
{ 
   int i; 
   for (i=O; i<n; ++i) 
     z[i] = (x[i] ^ ~y[i]) V (~x[i] ^ y[i]) 
} 
The set Z computed by the algorithm is:<image 1>
